  "id": "fair-sample",
  "after": "overview",
  "title": "A fair sample looks like the whole group.",
  "caption": "An imagined town of 100 people, where 30 drink coffee. A random sample (नमूना, namoona) of 10 picked from all over the town finds 3 coffee drinkers, 30%, just like the town. Ten people near the market, where the coffee drinkers live, give 80%. Same size, but the easy-to-reach sample is one-sided.",
  "alt": "Two copies of a 10 by 10 grid of dots for a town of 100 people; 30 red dots drink coffee and 70 blue dots drink chai, and most coffee drinkers live in the top-left corner near the market. Left: 10 people ringed from all over the town, 3 of them coffee drinkers, 30 percent, which matches the town. Right: a dashed box around 10 people in the market corner, 8 of them coffee drinkers, 80 percent, far from the truth.",
