  "id": "three-shapes",
  "after": "outcomes",
  "title": "Three common distributions.",
  "caption": "A distribution (बँटवारा, bantwara) shows how often each value appears. Heights pile up in a bell, the same on both sides of the mean: normal. The number of heads in 10 tosses is binomial: 5 heads is most likely, and 0 or 10 heads are very rare. A fair die is uniform: every face is equally likely.",
  "alt": "Three small charts. Normal: a smooth bell curve of adult heights from 150 to 190 centimetres, highest at 170. Binomial: eleven bars for 0 to 10 heads in 10 coin tosses, tallest at 5 and tiny at 0 and 10. Uniform: six equal bars for the faces 1 to 6 of a fair die.",
