  "title": "What to look for in the CLT lab.",
  "caption": "Household income is skewed (एकतरफ़ा, ektarfa): most homes earn a little and a few earn a lot. Averages of 5 homes (n = 5, the sample size) are less skewed. Averages of 30 homes form a narrow bell around the true mean (about ₹22k). The bars come from a computer simulation, and each panel's tallest bar is drawn the same height.",
  "alt": "Three histograms on the same income scale from 0 to 60 thousand rupees. Top: single household incomes, piled up on the left with a long tail to the right. Middle: averages of 5 homes, less lopsided and narrower. Bottom: averages of 30 homes, a narrow, even bell centred on the true mean of about 22 thousand rupees, marked by a dashed line through all three.",
