  "id": "die-average",
  "after": "selfCheck",
  "title": "The average of many rolls settles near 3.5.",
  "caption": "One computer run of 10,000 die (पासा, paasa) rolls. After 10 rolls the average was 4.1; after 10,000 it was 3.50, very close to the true 3.5. Your numbers will differ, but the line always settles down. The CLT lab shows the same idea: bigger samples give steadier averages.",
